      "heading": "A Northern Ireland care home answers to RQIA.",
      "text": "In Northern Ireland the regulator is the Regulation and Quality Improvement Authority, RQIA. CQC is England only. The Care Inspectorate is Scotland. RQIA registers and inspects residential and nursing homes under the Health and Personal Social Services (Quality, Improvement and Regulation) (Northern Ireland) Order 2003. It uses the Department of Health minimum care standards. It asks if care is safe, effective, compassionate and well led. So you need proof, dated, for each audit."
